{
"dur": 41.006,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 8.702,
"text": "May 2019. Warner Bros. names its new Batman, and within hours thousands of fans sign a petition to get him fired.",
"end": 8.977
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 8.977,
"vo_start": 9.252,
"vo_end": 17.848,
"text": "The complaint was simple. This was the sparkly vampire from Twilight. The boy who girls screamed at. Not a superhero.",
"end": 18.123
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 18.123,
"vo_start": 18.398,
"vo_end": 25.678,
"text": "Seven years later, on the sixteenth of November 2026, Amazon made an announcement. Robert Pattinson will be the next James Bond.",
"end": 25.953
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 25.953,
"vo_start": 26.228,
"vo_end": 36.068,
"text": "Same man. Same face. So what changed? Because Hollywood didn't hand him this. He spent fifteen years making sure they couldn't say no.",
"end": 36.343
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 36.343,
"vo_start": 36.618,
"vo_end": 40.056,
"text": "This is how a Twilight punchline became the most wanted actor in Hollywood.",
"end": 41.006
}
],
